hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"210","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What is Allah’s right over His servants? The people replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That people worship Allah and do not associate anyone with Him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When they do this, then what right will those people have over Allah? The people replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (It is that) Allah will forgive them and not punish them. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, there is a clear statement that those narrations which we have mentioned earlier are concise and not detailed, and some branches of faith are such that when a person commits them, Paradise does not become obligatory for him at all times. Have you not considered that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has declared Allah’s right over the servants to be that they worship Him and do not associate anyone with Him? And the worship of Allah is affirmation by the tongue, confirmation by the heart, and action by the limbs. Then, when the Muslims asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about their right over Allah, they asked: What right will those people have over Allah when they do this? They did not say: What right will those people have over Allah when they say this. And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not reject these words either. So, in what we have stated, there is a clear statement that Paradise does not become obligatory for a person who fulfills some branches of faith in all conditions; rather, every narration has its own generality, and the ruling has a specific context. As we have mentioned earlier."
"211","I woke up and saw that there was no one in front of the camel of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). I set out to search for the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and I saw Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) standing. I asked: Where is the Messenger of Allah? Both of them replied: We do not know, but we heard a sound coming from the upper part of the valley. It was like the sound of a millstone turning. The narrator says: We stayed there for a while, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us and said: An angel from my Lord came to me and gave me the choice between half of my Ummah entering Paradise without reckoning and intercession, or (absolutely) granting me intercession. So I chose intercession. The people said: O Messenger of Allah! We beseech you by Allah and by your companionship, include us among those who will be eligible for your intercession. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You will be eligible for my intercession. The narrator states: When those people mounted, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I make all those present here witnesses that my intercession will be granted to every individual of my Ummah who dies in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Allah."
"212","I saw every person present there weeping. The narrator says: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, began to say, I think that after this, whoever seeks permission from you will be foolish. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, stood up and praised and glorified Allah. Whenever he took an oath, he would say: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul.” (He said:) “I bear witness before Allah that whoever among you believes in Allah and then remains steadfast (i.e., continues to act upon Islamic commands), that person will enter Paradise. My Lord has promised me that He will admit seventy thousand individuals from my Ummah into Paradise without reckoning or punishment, and I hope that those people will not enter Paradise until you and your righteous wives and children reach your places in Paradise.” The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When half the night—(the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words)—when the night falls, Allah descends to the lowest heaven and says: I do not ask My servants about anyone other than Myself. Who is there who asks of Me, so I may grant him? Who is there who seeks forgiveness from Me, so I may forgive him? Who is there who supplicates to Me, so I may accept his supplication?” (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, says:) This continues until the break of dawn."
"213","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Jibreel came to me and gave me the glad tidings that whoever from my Ummah dies in"
"214","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) relating this from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Sayyiduna"
"215","""Allah laughs at two men, one of whom killed the other but they both entered Paradise. The first one fought in the cause of Allah and was killed, then Allah accepted the repentance of the one who killed him, and he fought and was martyred."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3166)"
"216","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and Abu Bakr ؓ became (caliph) after him, and some of the Arabs apostatized,ʻUmar ؓ said: O Abu Bakr, how can you fight the people when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿI have been ordered to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god except Allah. Whoever bears witness that there is no god except Allah has protected his wealth and his life from me, except in cases dictated by Islamic law, and their reckoning will be with Allahʿ? Abu Bakr ؓ said: by Allah I shall certainly fight the one who separates prayer and zakah, for zakah is what is due from wealth. By Allah, whoever withholds from me a goat that they used to give (in zakah) to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I shall fight them for withholding it. 'Umar said: By Allah, as soon as I realized that Allah had opened the heart of Abu Bakr to fighting, I realized that it was the right thing to do. (Using translation from Aḥmad 117)"
"217","""When the Messenger of Allah died, and Abu Bakr became the Khalifah after him, and some of the 'Arabs reverted to disbelief. 'umar said to Abu Bakr: 'How can you fight the people when the Messenger of allah said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship but Allah). Whoever says La ilaha illah, his wealth and his life safe from me, unless he deserves a legal punishment justly, and his reckoning will be with Allah?""' Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'I will fight anyone who separates prayer and Zakah; Zakah is the compulsory right to be taken from wealth. By Allah, if they withhold from me a rope that they used to give to the Messenger of Allah, I will fight them for wiholding it.' 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: 'By Allah, it was as if I saw that Allah has opened the heart of Abu Bakr for fighting, and I knew that I was the truth.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2443)"
"218","I have been commanded to fight against people so long as they do not declare that there is no god but Allah, and he who professed it was guaranteed the protection of his property and life on my behalf except for the right affairs rest with Allah. (Using translation from Muslim 21a)"
"219","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I have been ordered (by Allah) to fight against the people until they testify that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah and that Muhammad is Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and offer the prayers perfectly and give the obligatory charity, so if they perform that, then they save their lives and property from me except for Islamic laws and then their reckoning (accounts) will be done by Allah."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 25)"
"220","I have been commanded to fight against people, till they testify to the fact that there is no god but Allah, and believe in me (that) I am the messenger (from the Lord) and in all that I have brought. And when they do it, their blood and riches are guaranteed protection on my behalf except where it is justified by law, and their affairs rest with Allah. (Using translation from Muslim 21b)"
"221","I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, and I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness before Allah that whoever among the believing servants comes before Allah with these two statements, then these two things will become a means of salvation from Hell for that person on the Day of Resurrection.” Sayyiduna Abu Amrah Ansari’s name is Thalabah bin Amr bin Muhsin."
"222","The people of Paradise will enter Paradise, and the people of Hell will enter Hell. Then Allah Almighty will say: Review those people—whoever you find in his heart even a mustard seed's weight of faith, take him out (from Hell).” The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: “So those people will come out of Hell in such a state that, after being burnt, they will have become like charcoal. They will be thrown into the River of Life, and they will burst forth from it just as a seed bursts forth on the bank of a flood stream.” The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Have you not seen it, how it is yellow in color and sways here and there?”"
"223","I lead the people of my neighborhood in prayer. When it rains, water flows between me and those people in the lower part (of the area), so I cannot reach their mosque to lead them in prayer. Therefore, O Messenger of Allah! I wish that you would come (to my house) and offer prayer at some place in my house, so that I may make that place my prayer area. The narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will do so soon. Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) came after the sun had risen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission to enter. I granted you permission. After entering the house, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not sit down first. He said: Where in your house do you like that I should offer prayer? The narrator says: I pointed to a corner of the house, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood there and said the takbeer. We stood behind you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in two rak’ahs of prayer and then made salaam. The narrator says: We detained you to eat khazeerah (a special type of food) which we had prepared for you. The narrator says: Some people from the neighborhood also gathered around the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until several people gathered in the house. One of them said: Where is Malik bin Dukhshun? Then another said: He is a hypocrite; he does not love Allah and His Messenger. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to that person: Do not say this about him. Have you not seen that he said: There is no god but Allah? He said this word seeking the pleasure of Allah. The people said: Allah and His Messenger know best. We have only noted that his attention and goodwill are for the hypocrites. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah has made the Fire of Hell forbidden for the person who says ‘La ilaha illallah’ seeking the pleasure of Allah.” Ibn Shihab says: I asked Husayn bin Muhammad Ansari about this; he is a man from Banu Salim and among their elders. I asked him about the narration of Sayyiduna Mahmood bin Rabee’ (may Allah be pleased with him), and he confirmed this narration."
"224","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'No one will enter Paradise who has even a mustard-seed's weight of arrogance in his heart, and no one will enter Hell who has even a mustard-seed's weight of faith in his heart.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 59)"
"225","“A man from my nation will be called before all of creation on the Day of Resurrection, and ninety-nine scrolls will be spread out for him, each one extending as far as the eye can see. Then Allah will say: “Do you deny anything of this?” He will say: “No, O Lord.” He will say: “Have My recording scribes been unfair to you?” Then He will say: “Apart from that, do you have any good deeds?” The man will be terrified and will say: “No.” (Allah) will say: “Indeed, you have good deeds with Us, and you will not be treated unjustly this Day.” Then a card will be brought out on which is written Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammadan ‘abduhu wa rasuluhu (I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, and that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger). He will say: “O Lord, what is this card compared with these scrolls?” He will say: “You will not be treated unjustly.” Then the scrolls will be placed in one side of the Balance and the card in the other. The scrolls will go up (i.e., be light) and the card will go down (i.e., will weigh heavily).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4300)"
"226","I will meet you with forgiveness as much as the earth."
"227","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people who will be given a double reward. A person from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, and then lived to see the time of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), believed in him and followed him, he will have a double reward. A slave who fulfills the right of Allah upon him and also fulfills the right of his master upon him, he too will have a double reward. And a person who has a slave-girl, provides her with good food, gives her good education and upbringing, then frees her and marries her, he will also have a double reward."" Imam Shabi said to the man from Khurasan: ""You have obtained this hadith without any compensation, otherwise previously, for a narration of lesser content than this, one had to travel all the way to Madinah Munawwarah."
"228","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person's Islam becomes good, then every good deed he does is rewarded for him from ten times up to seven hundred times, and every evil deed that he commits is recorded as one evil deed, until that person appears before Allah, the Exalted."
"229","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Of the perfection of one's Islam, is that he leaves that which does not concern him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3976)"
"230","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""A Muslim is the one who avoids harming Muslims with his tongue and hands. And a Muhajir (emigrant) is the one who gives up (abandons) all what Allah has forbidden."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 10)"
"231","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Indeed, a believer for another believer is like a building, one part of which strengthens the other."
"232","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the believers in their mutual love is like a building."" The narrator says, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers and said: ""One part of it supports the other."
"233","The example of the believer is like that of a body; when one part of it suffers, the whole body feels that pain."
"234","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""None of you will have faith till he wishes for his (Muslim) brother what he likes for himself."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 13)"
"235","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""A servant cannot attain the reality of faith until he likes for people that goodness which he likes for himself."
"236","By him in whose hand my soul is, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another: should I not guide you to something doing which you will love one another: spread out salutation among you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5193)"
"237","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""There are three things, whoever has them will taste the sweetness of faith. That a person loves Allah and His Messenger more than anything else besides them; that he loves a people only for the sake of Allah; and that he would rather be thrown into the fire than return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it.\"""""""
"238","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""There are three qualities, whoever possesses them will taste the sweetness of faith: One is that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; (second) that he loves a person and he loves him only for the sake of Allah; and (third) that he hates to return to disbelief just as he would hate to be thrown into the fire.\"""""""
"239","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Three things are obligatory upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending the funeral, and when a person who sneezes says 'Alhamdulillah', to respond to him."
"240","“The Muslim has four things due from the Muslim: He should answer [by saying Yarhamuk-Allah (may Allah have mercy on you)] to him if he sneezes (and says Al-Hamdulillah); he should accept his invitation if he invites him; he should attend his funeral if he dies; and he should visit him if he falls sick.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1434)"
"241","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: A Muslim has five rights over another Muslim: returning the greeting of salam, visiting the sick, accompanying the funeral, accepting invitations, and responding to one who sneezes."
"242","The people asked: “O Messenger of Allah! What are they?” He replied: “When he meets him, he should greet him with salam; when he invites him, he should accept his invitation; when he seeks his advice, he should advise him sincerely; when he sneezes and praises Allah, he should respond to him; when he is ill, he should visit him; and when he dies, he should accompany his funeral.”"
"243","The narrator says: I think the words in the narration are: more beloved than red camels."
"244","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were sitting with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). During that time, \""Jumar\"" (the gum of the date-palm tree) was brought, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: There is a tree whose blessing is like that of a Muslim. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I thought that it would be the date-palm tree. Then I looked at those present, and I was the tenth person among ten people th"
"245","One day the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said to his companions: Tell me about a tree whose example is like that of a believing servant"
"246","There is a tree amongst trees, the leaves of which do not wither and that is like a Muslim; tell me which that (tree) can be? The people began to think of the trees of the forest. Abdullah said: I thought that it could be the date-palm tree, but I felt hesitant (to say that). They (the Companions) then said: Messenger of Allah, (kindly) tell us which that can be? Thereupon he said: It is the date-palm tree. I made a mention of that to 'Umar, whereupon he said: Had you said that it meant the date-palin tree, this statement of yours (would have been dearer to me) than such and such things. (Using translation from Muslim 2811a)"
"247","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a believer is like that of a date palm tree, which only consumes pure things and only gives pure things."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The narrator named Shu’bah made a mistake in narrating the name of the narrator as ""Adas."" The correct word is ""Hadas,"" as narrated by Hammad bin Salamah and other authorities."
"248","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a person calls another person a disbeliever, then that disbelief returns to one of the two. If the (other person) is indeed a disbeliever (then it is correct), otherwise the first person, due to calling him a disbeliever, himself becomes a disbeliever."
"249","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If anyone says to his brother, 'O misbeliever! Then surely, one of them such."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6104)"
"250","Any person who called his brother: ""O unbeliever"" (has in fact done an act by which this unbelief) would return to one of them. If it were so, as he asserted (then the unbelief of man was confirmed but if it was not true), then it returned to him (to the man who labeled it on his brother Muslim). (Using translation from Muslim 60b)"
"251","I heard from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and the other I say myself. I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever presents himself before Allah in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Allah, then Allah will admit him into Paradise."
"252","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Then his father will become extremely ugly and extremely foul-smelling, so that person will leave him. Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, states: The companions of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, used to think: This is about Sayyiduna Ibrahim, peace be upon him. However, the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, did not use more words than these (which have already been mentioned in this narration)."
"253","I met A'mash, and he also narrated this hadith to me."
"254","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Whoever has (the following) four characteristics will be a pure hypocrite: ""If he speaks, he tells a lie; if he gives a promise, he breaks it, if he makes a covenant he proves treacherous; and if he quarrels, he behaves in a very imprudent evil insulting manner (unjust). And whoever has one of these characteristics, has one characteristic of a hypocrite, unless he gives it us."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3178)"
"255","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever possesses four traits will be a pure hypocrite. When he speaks, he lies; when he makes a promise, he breaks it; when he makes a covenant, he violates it; and when he quarrels, he behaves in an obscene manner. And whoever possesses any one of these traits, he has a trait of hypocrisy in him.”"""""
"257","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Three ˹traits˺ that if one possesses them is a hypocrite – even if he fasts, prays, and claims to be a Muslim: one who (1) when he speaks, he lies, (2) when he promises, he breaks it, and (3) when he is entrusted, he betrays."""""
"258","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever, without a valid excuse, misses three Friday prayers is a hypocrite.”"
"259","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the prayer of the hypocrites. One of them keeps delaying the prayer until the sun is between the two horns of Satan, then he stands up and pecks four times (performs the prayer hastily), and he remembers Allah very little in that prayer."
"260","I not tell you about the prayer of the hypocrites? He does not perform the Asr prayer until, when the sun is between the two horns of Satan (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or until it reaches the horn of Satan, then he pecks at it like a rooster. He remembers Allah very little in this prayer."
"261","We came upon Anas b. Malik after the Zuhr prayer. He stood for saying the 'Asr prayer. When he became free from praying, we mentioned to him about observing prayer in its early period or he himself mentioned it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: This is how hypocrites pray, this is how hypocrites pray, this is how hypocrites pray: He sits (watching the sun), and when it becomes yellow and is between the horns of the devil, or is on the horns of the devil, he rises and prays for rak'ahs quickly, remembering Allah only seldom during them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 413)"
"262","'Have you prayed 'Asr?' We said: 'No, we have just finished Zuhr.' He said: 'Pray 'Asr.' So we got up and prayed, and when we finished he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""That is the prayer of the hypocrite: he sits and delays 'Asr prayer until (the sun) is between the horns of the Shaitan, then he gets up and pecks four (Rak'ahs) in which he only remembers Allah a little.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 511)"
"263","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) after the Zuhr prayer. He inquired: Have you performed the Asr prayer? We replied: No. He said: Perform the prayer here in our room. When we finished the prayer, Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) performed a lengthy prayer. After completing his prayer, he turned towards us, and the very first thing he said to us was that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the prayer of the hypocrites. One of them sits and waits until, when the sun is between the horns of Satan (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or reaches between the two horns of Satan, then he stands up and pecks four times (i.e., prays quickly), and in those rak‘ahs he remembers Allah very little."",""In English"",""it translates to: """"He prayed with us in the room"","" then he finished and lengthened his stay"","" and finally he turned towards us. The first thing he said to us was that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'That is the prayer of the hypocrites. One of them sits until it is almost time for the prayer to end"","" then he quickly stands up and makes four quick rak'ahs"","" in which he hardly remembers Allah.'"""""""""
"264","I am not rejecting your statement, but when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said this, I was present with him. He said this. Upon this, Abdullah bin Safwan asked: O Abu Abdur Rahman! What did the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say? So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: (For the herd) the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used the word ""Rabidain"" (whereas you used the word ""Ghanamain""). Then Ubaid bin Umair or perhaps Abdullah bin Safwan said: O Abu Abdur Rahman! The meaning of both ""Rabidain"" and ""Ghanamain"" is the same. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard it in this way, I heard it in this way. I heard it in this way. (The narrator states) Whenever Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) heard any word from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), he would neither add to it nor subtract from it."
"265","I saw the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he placed his thumb on his ear and his finger, with which he gestures during prayer, on his eye. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The meaning of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, placing his finger on his ears and his eyes is: to clarify to the people that Allah, the Exalted, does not hear by means of an ear that has a hole and a curve, nor does He see with the help of an eye that has pupils, eyeballs, and whiteness. Our Lord is far above and exalted from being likened to anything from His creation; rather, He hears and sees without any instrument, as He wills."
"266","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not sleep, and it does not befit His Majesty that He should sleep. He lowers and raises the scales. The deeds of the day are presented before Him before the coming of the night, and the deeds of the night before the coming of the day. His veil is light. If He were to remove the veil, the radiance of His countenance would burn everything that His sight reaches. He has extended His hand of mercy during the night for the sinner of the day, so that He may accept his repentance during the day, and He has extended His hand during the day for the sinner of the night, so that He may accept his repentance during the night."" (This will continue) until the sun rises from the west."
"267","""Allah, the Mighty and Sublinm, says: 'The son of Adam denied Me and he had no right to do so. and the son of Adam reviled Me and he had no right to do so. As for his denying Me, It is his saying that I will not resurrect him as I created him in the beginning, but resurrecting him is not more difficult for Me than creating him in the first place. And as for his reviling Me, it is his saying that Allah has taken a son, but I am Allah, the One, the Self-Sufficient Master, I beget not nor was I begotten, and there is none co-equal or comparable unto Me.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2078)"
"268","The reason for this is: The Arabs sometimes use the word 'foot' in their language to mean 'place,' as in the statement of Allah Almighty: 'For them will be a place of truth with their Lord.' What is meant by this is a place of truth; it does not mean that Allah Almighty will place His foot in Hell. Our Lord is exalted and far above this and similar things."
"269","Verily, Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, would say on the Day of Resurrection: O son of Adam, I was sick but you did not visit Me. He would say: O my Lord; how could I visit Thee whereas Thou art the Lord of the worlds? Thereupon He would say: Didn't you know that such and such servant of Mine was sick but you did not visit him and were you not aware of this that if you had visited him, you would have found Me by him? O son of Adam, I asked food from you but you did not feed Me. He would say: My Lord, how could I feed Thee whereas Thou art the Lord of the worlds? He said: Didn't you know that such and such servant of Mine asked food from you but you did not feed him, and were you not aware that if you had fed him you would have found him by My side? (The Lord would again say: ) O son of Adam, I asked drink from you but you did not provide Me. He would say: My Lord, how could I provide Thee whereas Thou art the Lord of the worlds? Thereupon He would say: Such and such of servant of Mine asked you for a drink but you did not provide him, and had you provided him drink you would have found him near Me. (Using translation from Muslim 2569)"
"270","The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Exactly as if he placed it in the hand of the Most Merciful."" This clarifies for you that in these narrations, the words of example are used; it is not intended that the reality of it exists or that its nature is known, because the addressee can only understand these things through the words to which their application is made."
"271","that the Prophet ﷺ said, ""Guarantee for me six ˹deeds˺ from yourselves and I will guarantee for you Paradise: (1) Be truthful when you speak, (2) keep your promises when you make them, (3) fulfill the trust when you are entrusted, (4) guard your chastity, (5) lower your gaze, and (6) restrain your hands ˹from harming others.˺"" (Using translation from Aḥmad 22757)"
"272","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A man keeps speaking the truth, and strives to speak the truth, until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful person. And a person keeps telling lies, and strives to tell lies, until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."
"273","Truth leads one to Paradise and virtue leads one to Paradise and the person tells the truth until he is recorded as truthful, and lie leads to obscenity and obscenity leads to Hell, and the person tells a lie until he is recorded as a liar. (Using translation from Muslim 2607a)"
"274","Avoid falsehood, for falsehood leads to wickedness, and wickedness to hell; and if a man continues to speak falsehood and makes falsehood his object, he will be recorded in Allah’s presence as a great liar. And adhere to truth, for truth leads to good deeds, and good deeds lead to paradise. If a man continues to speak the truth and makes truth his object, he will be recorded in Allah’s presence as eminently truthful. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4989)"
"275","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Beware! The fear of people should not prevent anyone from speaking the truth, when a person sees that it is necessary to speak the truth here."
"276","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah along with the displeasure of people, Allah becomes pleased with him, and makes the people pleased with him as well. And whoever seeks the pleasure of people along with the displeasure of Allah, Allah becomes displeased with him, and makes the people displeased with him as well."
"277","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever pleases Allah while displeasing the people, Allah becomes sufficient for him; and whoever displeases Allah to please the people, Allah hands him over to the people."
"278","The fear of people should not prevent any person from speaking the truth, when a man sees it or knows that (it is appropriate to speak the truth here)."" Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Trials kept befalling us continuously, until we fell short. Now we are in a bad situation."
"279","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, we were made up of nine; five and four. The first of the numbers for the Arabs, and the latter for the non-Arabs. He said: 'Listen, have you heard that after me there will leaders, whoever enters upon them and condones to their lies, and supports them in their oppression, then he is not from me and I am not from him, and he shall not drink with me from the Hawd. And whoever does not enter upon them, nor help them in their oppression, nor condones to their lies, then he is from me, and I am from him, and he shall drink with me at the Hawd.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2259)"
"280","“You have kinship and rights, and I see you entering upon these rulers and speaking to them as Allah wills you should speak. But i heard Bilal bin Harith Al-Muzani, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘One of you may speak a word that pleases Allah, and not know how far it reaches, but Allah will record for him as pleasure, until the Day of Resurrection due to that word. And one of you may speak a word that angers Allah, and not know how far it reaches, but Allah will record against him his anger, until the Day he meets Him due to that word.” 'Alqamah said: ""So look, woe to you, at what you say and what you speak about, for there is something that I wanted to say but I refrained because of what I heard from Bilal bin Harith."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3969)"
"281","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, one of you says a word that is pleasing to Allah, and he does not realize how far it will reach, but Allah records His pleasure for him because of that word until the day he will meet Allah. And a person says a word that is displeasing to Allah: he does not realize how far it will reach, but Allah records His displeasure for him because of that word until the day he will meet Allah.”"
"282","""The Messenger of Allah came out to us, and there were nine of us. He said; 'After me there will be rulers, whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Cistern. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of hi, and he will come to me at the Cistern.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4207)"
"283","""The Messenger of Allah came out to us, and there were nine of us. He said; 'After me there will be rulers, whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Cistern. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of hi, and he will come to me at the Cistern.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4207)"
"284","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Listen attentively! We said: We are ready to listen. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Listen attentively! We said: We are ready to listen. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Soon after me, some rulers will come, so do not affirm their lies and do not help them in their oppression, because whoever affirms their lies and helps them in their oppression will not be able to reach my pond.'"
"285","""The Messenger of Allah came out to us, and there were nine of us. He said; 'After me there will be rulers, whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Cistern. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of hi, and he will come to me at the Cistern.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4207)"
"286","I am free from him and he is free from me. And whoever does not affirm their lies and does not help them in their oppression, I am connected to him and he is connected to me."
"287","Sayyiduna Bilal bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him), who is a companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him), narrate: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""A servant utters a word, and he does not realize how far it will reach; because of that word, Allah writes His pleasure for that servant until the Day of Resurrection. And a servant utters a word, and he does not realize how far it will reach; but because of that word, Allah writes His displeasure for that person until the Day of Resurrection."" So, O my nephew! Consider what you say and what you speak about. Since I heard this from Sayyiduna Bilal bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him), I have refrained from speaking carelessly."
"288","l saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do wudoo’after minor impurity and he wiped over the khuffain. (Using translation from Aḥmad 128)"
"289","The narrator says) He went to that person and he gave him a gift. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever guides towards goodness, then for him is a reward like that of the one who acts upon it (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) like the one who acts upon it.”"
"290","I realized that he was not in a good mood. He performed ablution and did not talk to anyone. Then he went outside. I stood by the door of the chamber so that I could hear what he would say: He sat on the pulpit, praised and glorified Allah Almighty, then said: O people! Indeed, Allah the Blessed and Exalted has commanded you to enjoin good and forbid evil. Before you ask me for supplication and I do not accept your supplication, before you ask me for something and I do not grant it to you, before you ask me for help and I do not help you. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) only said these words, and then descended from the pulpit."
"291","narrates: She heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saying this from the pulpit: ""There is nothing more possessive of honor than Allah, the Exalted."
"292","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A believer is possessive (protective), and Allah Almighty is even more intensely possessive."
"293","Allah is self-respecting and a believer is also self-respecting and the respect of Allah is injured if a believer does what He has forbidden him to do. (Using translation from Muslim 2761a)"
"294","Nothing is more loveable to Allah than His praise as He has praised Himself and no one is more self-respecting than Allah Himself and it As because of this that He has prohibited abominable acts. (Using translation from Muslim 2760a)"
"295","The Prophet ﷺ said: There is jealousy which Allah loves and jealousy which Allah hates. That which Allah loves is jealousy regarding a matter of doubt, and that which Allah hates is jealousy regarding something which is not doubtful. There is pride which Allah hates and pride which Allah loves. That which Allah loves is a man's pride when fighting and when giving sadaqah and that which Allah hates is pride shown by oppression. The narrator Musa said: ""by boasting."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2659)"
"296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not get angry."
"297","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying this on the pulpit. He said: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and"
"298","The example of the one who violates the limits set by Allah and the one who observes them, the one who commands it and the one who forbids it, is like a group of people who drew lots for their places in a boat on the sea. One of them got the rear part of the boat. That person is distant from his companions, and those people are foolish. Whenever people come there, they cause him trouble, so those people say, ‘We are closer to convenience among all the people of the boat and farther from the water, so come, let us break the lower part of the boat. When we are done with it, we will fix it back.’ Then, among them, the foolish person says, ‘Go ahead and do it,’ and he moves towards the axe to strike it on the floor of the boat. Then a wise person peeks at him and asks, ‘What are you doing?’ He says, ‘We are closer to convenience than you and farther from it than you. I am about to break the plank of the boat. When our need is fulfilled, we will close it back.’ So the wise person says, ‘Do not do this. If you do this, you will be destroyed and we too will be destroyed.’”"
"299","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory to give charity for every joint of the children of Adam every day."" One of those present asked: Who has the ability to do this? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, helping a weak person by lifting his load is charity, and when any one of you walks towards the prayer, every step of his is charity."
"300","The Prophet ﷺ said: If any man is among a people in whose midst he does acts of disobedience, and, though they are able to make him change (his acts), they do not change, Allah will smite them with punishment before they die. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4339)"
"301","The example of the one who violates the limits set by Allah and the one who enforces them and prevents their violation is like a group of people who drew lots for places on a boat at sea. Some of them got the lower part of the boat. Those people were farther from convenience, and some went to the upper part. When those in the lower part wanted to get water, they had to pass by those above, causing them inconvenience. So one of them said: We are closer to convenience and farther from water. Let us break a part of the boat and get water directly. When our need is fulfilled, we will close it up again. Among them, some foolish people said: Go ahead and do it. So one of them took an axe and struck the floor of the boat. Then one wise person among them said: What are you doing? He replied: We are closer to convenience and farther from water, so we are breaking the floor of the boat to get water. When our need is fulfilled, we will close it up again. The wise person said: Do not do this, for if you do, you will be destroyed and we will also be destroyed.”"
"302","The Prophet ﷺ said: If any man is among a people in whose midst he does acts of disobedience, and, though they are able to make him change (his acts), they do not change, Allah will smite them with punishment before they die. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4339)"
"303","I have removed it.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I think we have caused you hardship, we have caused you harm.” Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The narrator named Nu’man bin Rashid sometimes makes mistakes when narrating hadith from Zuhri."
"304","O people, you recite this verse: ʿO you who believe! Take care of your own selves. If you follow the (right) guidance [and enjoin what is right (Islamic Monotheism and all that Islam orders one to do) and forbid what is wrong (polytheism, disbelief and all that Islam has forbidden)] no hurt can come to you from those who are in errorʿ [al-Ma’idah 5:105]. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If the people see an evildoer and do not stop him, soon Allah will send His punishment upon them all.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 30)"
"305","0 people, you recite this verse but you quote it inappropriately: “O you who believe! Take care of your own selves. If you follow the (right) guidance [and enjoin what is right (Islamic Monotheism and all that Islam orders one to do) and forbid what is wrong (polytheism, disbelief and all that Islam has forbidden)] no hurt can come to you from those who are in errorʿ (al-Ma'idah 5:105]. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ʿIf the people see evil and do not denounce it, soon Allah will send His punishment upon them ali.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 53)"
"306","""The first to advance the Khutbah before the Salat was Marwan. A man stood to say to Marwan: 'You have contradicted the Sunnah.' So he said: 'O so-and-so! What was there it has been left.' So Abu Sa'eed said: 'As for this, he has fulfilled what is upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whomever among you sees an evil, then let him stop it with his hand. Whomever is not able,then with his tongue, and whomever is not able, then with his heart. That is the weakest of faith.""' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2172)"
"307","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say:) ""Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand; if he is not able to do so, then with his tongue; and if he is not able to do so, then with his heart—and that is the weakest level of faith."
"308","""Whoever spends on a pair (of things) in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, he will be called in Paradise: 'O slave of Allah, here is prosperity, Whoever is one of the people of Salah, he will be called from the gate of salah. Whoever is on of the people of charity, he will be called from the gate of Ar-Rayyan.' Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said: 'O Messenger of Allah, no distress or need will befall the one who is called from those gates. Will there be anyone who will be called from all these gates?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2238)"
"309","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Every letter in the Qur'an in which the mention of 'Qunoot' is found, by it is meant obedience."
"310","""I heard Mu'awiyah bin Abu Sufyan narrating that the Messenger of Allah said: ""Goodness is a (natural) habit while evil is a stubbornness (constant prodding from Satan). When Allah wills good for a person, He causes him to understand the religion.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 221)"
"311","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood (in prayer) until his feet became swollen. It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.’ He said: ‘Should I not be a thankful slave?’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1419)"
"312","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not regularly perform the Duha prayer, whereas Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to perform this prayer. She used to say: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would abandon many actions for fear that people might start following that way and it might become obligatory upon them."
"313","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would sometimes abandon a certain deed even though he liked to act upon it, out of concern that people would also start doing that deed and it would become obligatory upon them."
"314","There were three persons in Bani Isra'il, one suffering from leprosy, the other bald-headed and the third one blind. Allah decided to test them. So He sent an angel who came to the one who was suffering from leprosy and said: Which thing do you like most? He said: Beautiful colour and fine skin and removal of that which makes me detestable in the eye of people. He wiped him and his illness was no more and he was conferred upon beautiful colour and beautiful skin. He (the angel) again said: Which property do you like most? He said: Camels, or he said: The cow the narrator is, however, doubtful about it, but (out of the persons) suffering from leprosy or baldness one of them definitely said: The camel. And the other one said: Cow. And he (one who demanded camel) was bestowed upon a she-camel, in an advanced stage of pregnancy, and while giving he said: May Allah bless you in this. Then he came to the bald-headed person and said: Which thing do you like most? He said: Beautiful hair and that (this baldness) may be removed from me because of which people hate me. He wiped his body and his illness was removed and he was bestowed upon beautiful hair, and the angel said: Which wealth do you like most? He said: The cow. And he was given a pregnant cow and while handing it over to him he (the angel) said: May Allah bless you in this. Then he came to the blind man and he said: Which thing do you like most? He said: Allah should restore my eyesight so that I should be able to see people with the help of that. He wiped his body and Allah restored to him his eyesight, and he (the angel) also said: Which wealth do you like most? He said: The flock of sheep. And he was given a pregnant goat and that gave birth to young ones and it so happened that one valley abounded in camels and the other one in cows and the third one in sheep. He then came to the one who had suffered from leprosy in his (old) form and shape and he said: I am a poor person and my provision has run short in my journey and there is none to take me to my destination except with the help of Allah and your favour. I beg of you in His name Who gave you fine colour and fine skin, and the camel in the shape of wealth (to confer upon me) a camel which should carry me in my journey. He said: I have many responsibilities to discharge. Thereupon he said: I perceive as if I recognise you. Were you not suffering from leprosy whom people hated and you were a destitute and Allah conferred upon you (wealth)? He said: I have inherited this property from my forefathers. Thereupon he said: If you are a liar may Allah change you to that very position in which you had been. He then came to the one who was bald-headed in his (old) form and said to him the same what he had said to him (one suffering from leprosy) and he gave him the same reply as he had given him and he said: If you are a liar, may Allah turn you to your previous position in which you had been. And then he came to the blind man in his (old) form and shape and he said: I am a destitute person and a wayfarer. My provision have ran short and today there is no way to reach the destination but with the help of Allah and then with your help and I beg of you in the (name) of One Who restored your eyesight and gave you the flock of sheep to give me a sheep by which I should be able to make my provisions for the journey. He said: I was blind and Allah restored to me my eyesight; you take whatever you like and leave whatever you like. By Allah, I shall not stand in your way today for what you take in the name of God. Thereupon, he said: You keep with you what you have (in your possession). The fact is that you three were put to test and Allah is well pleased with you and He is annoyed with your companions. (Using translation from Muslim 2964)"
"315","""The one who eats and is grateful is like the status of the patient fasting person."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2486)"
"316","The wife of Sayyiduna Uthman bin Maz'un (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The wives saw that her outward appearance was not good, so they asked: What has happened to you? Among the Quraysh, there is no one more prosperous than your husband. The woman replied: We have nothing to do with him. He fasts during the day and spends the night in voluntary prayers. Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came home, and the pure wives mentioned this matter before him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Sayyiduna Uthman bin Maz'un (may Allah be pleased with him), and said: O Uthman! Is there not an example for you in my way? He asked: What has happened, O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You spend the whole night in voluntary prayers and fast during the day? Your wife has a right over you. Your body has a right over you. Pray voluntary prayers at night and also sleep, and fast during the day and also do not fast. The narrator says: After this, his wife came to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she had applied perfume as if she were a bride. The wives asked her: What happened? She replied: We have also received what the people have received."
"317","A group of three men came to the houses of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ asking how the Prophet ﷺ worshipped (Allah), and when they were informed about that, they considered their worship insufficient and said, ""Where are we from the Prophet ﷺ as his past and future sins have been forgiven."" Then one of them said, ""I will offer the prayer throughout the night forever."" The other said, ""I will fast throughout the year and will not break my fast."" The third said, ""I will keep away from the women and will not marry forever."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and said, ""Are you the same people who said so-and-so? By Allah, I am more submissive to Allah and more afraid of Him than you; yet I fast and break my fast, I do sleep and I also marry women. So he who does not follow my tradition in religion, is not from me (not one of my followers). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5063)"
"318","Are your parents living? He said: Yes. Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: You should put in your best efforts (in their) service. (Using translation from Muslim 2549a)"
"319","I recited seven long surahs (in voluntary prayers) last night."
"320","I am fasting. Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I swear that you must eat, for I will not eat until you eat. The narrator states that Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) then ate with him. Then he stayed with him that night. When night came, Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) got up to perform voluntary prayers, but Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) stopped him. He said: O Abu Darda! Your Lord has a right over you, your wife has a right over you, and your body has a right over you. Give each one who has a right their due. Fast sometimes and leave it sometimes. Pray voluntary prayers and also sleep. And go to your wife as well. When the time of true dawn approached, Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Now get up. Then both of them got up, performed voluntary prayers, and went to perform the obligatory prayer. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had performed the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him and informed him about what Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) had said. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) then said to him the same thing that Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) had said."
"321","“When the last ten days of Ramadan began, the Prophet ﷺ used to stay up at night, tighten his waist- wrap, and wake up his family (to pray).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1768)"
"322","The practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to be regular."
"323","The most beloved action to Messenger of Allah ﷺ was that whose doer did it continuously and regularly. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6462)"
"324","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There is no virtue more to the liking of Allah in any day than in these days, that is, the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. They (the Companions) asked: Messenger of Allah, not even the struggle in the path of Allah (Jihad) ? He said: (Yes), not even the struggle in the path of Allah, except a man who goes out (in the path of Allah) with his life and property, and does not return with any of them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2438)"
